    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-043: Box Shadow**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (3 commits, ~200 lines) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n**Honest infrastructure-first cycle.** 19 rules use `box-shadow` in Wikipedia CSS, but only 1 produces a static first-viewport delta (a 1px line under the toolbar container).\n\n## Measurement (Wikipedia CSS, 2026-10-28)\n\n| Type | Count | Renders statically? |\n|---|---|---|\n| `inset 0 0 0 1px` focus rings (`:focus`) | **13** | ❌ Needs `:focus` state (ADR-018 is paint-only) |\n| `inset 2.75em 0 0` code-line highlights | 2 | ❌ Inside `<pre>` blocks (second-viewport) |\n| `box-shadow: none` no-ops | 2 | N/A |\n| `.vector-dropdown-content { 0 2px 6px }` | 1 | ❌ `visibility: hidden` |\n| **`.vector-page-toolbar-container { 0 1px #c8ccd1 }`** | **1** | ✅ First-viewport, non-inset |\n\n**Expected visible delta: 1 line** — or **0** if the toolbar already has a border.\n\n## Scope\n\n### Commit 1 (parse + layout, behavior-neutral)\n- `LayoutBox` gains 7 box-shadow fields\n- `box-shadow` shorthand parse (ox oy blur spread color + optional inset)\n- `box-shadow: none` clears fields\n- Multi-shadow: first only (deferred)\n- Zero paint changes — no visible delta yet\n\n### Commit 2 (paint, visible)\n- `paint_box` draws shadow before background fill\n- Skips inset and blur (v1 deferred render)\n- **PNG verification gate before merge**\n- **CRITICAL pre-check**: does the toolbar already have a border? If so, shadow may be invisible → honest \"0 visible\" accounting, not silent failure\n\n### Commit 3 (docs)\n- ADR-043 → Implemented\n- ADR-034 post-note (shadow + background draw order)\n- README + CHANGELOG\n\n## Why ship a cycle with at most 1px visible delta\n\n1. **Genuine infrastructure** — many sites use simple drop-shadows on cards/modals/buttons. Non-inset, sometimes no blur.\n2. **Foundation for `border-radius + box-shadow` combined cycle** — shadows on rounded boxes are the modern UI shape.\n3. **Parse-before-render discipline** — parsing all forms (inset, blur, multi) means future render-only changes don't need re-parsing.\n4. **1px is real** — as long as we verify it (or honestly document 0 if toolbar already bordered), the delta is measurable.\n\n## Deferred (documented in ADR)\n\n- Inset render (13 rules, all `:focus` state — needs layout recalc on state change)\n- Blur > 0 render (1 rule, `visibility: hidden`)\n- Multi-shadow (3 rules, all `:focus` state)\n- Transitions\n- Percentages in offsets\n- Inline-element shadows\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Infrastructure-first framing is honest** — 1px (or 0px) visible delta, full box-shadow pipeline shipped. Same shape as ADR-041 Commit 1 (parse+cascade, 0 visible delta) — precedent established. Agree?\n- [ ] **Parse-but-skip for inset and blur** — parsed and stored, not rendered. Preserves the chain for future implementation (paint-only change later). Alternative (reject at parse) requires re-parsing later. Agree?\n- [ ] **First-shadow-only for multi-shadow** — 3 Wikipedia rules use comma-lists, all `:focus` state. Cost of full-list parse is larger; benefit today is zero. Agree?\n- [ ] **PNG verification gate** — Commit 2 must show toolbar line OR confirm toolbar already bordered (in which case delta is 0 and that's documented, not silent). Agree?\n- [ ] **`clip_children` interaction** — ADR-039's Cairo clip happens after shadow draw, so shadows escape their own box's `overflow: hidden`. Matches CSS spec. But if a future ADR shifts this order, could regress. Flagged in ADR-043 Consequences. Agree?\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched. Post-merge: `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` — 539 / 2064 unchanged.\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/043-box-shadow.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #211",
